# Shell scripts run under bash on Linux/Docker — they MUST be checked out with LF.
# On the shared NTFS drive a CRLF checkout otherwise breaks them at runtime
# (e.g. `set -o pipefail\r` → invalid option; syntax error near `}`), which silently
# defeated the ISSUE-312 aborted-run guard in scripts/run-backend-tests.sh (see ISSUE-323).
*.sh text eol=lf

# Append-only ledgers: use git's union merge driver.
#
# Six concurrent PRs in one session each appended findings to TEST-FINDINGS.md and
# index lines to an agent MEMORY.md. Git's default three-way merge treats these as
# prose and conflicts on every pair, so each merge dirtied every other open PR — a
# cascade that cost more time than the work itself. Every one of those conflicts
# resolved to "keep both sides", because these files are logs, not documents.
#
# `union` is SAFE here precisely because nothing ever edits an existing entry:
# a finding is appended and later amended in place by a single owner, and a memory
# index only grows.
#
# GAP-CLOSURE-QUEUE.md is deliberately NOT listed. Ticking an item REWRITES an
# existing row, and union would keep both the ticked and unticked copies — silently
# duplicating queue rows. That file must keep conflicting so a human resolves it.
docs/QA/TEST-FINDINGS.md            merge=union
docs/QA/TEST-FINDINGS-RESOLVED.md   merge=union
.claude/agent-memory/**/MEMORY.md   merge=union
